From 92b14b8b261801069a368035904967abe0139761 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:10:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/70] CUDA/HIP: fold the conv-state concat, snapshot copies
 and gather into SSM_CONV

build_conv_state runs per linear-attention layer a GET_ROWS of the conv
state, a CONCAT with the transposed new inputs, one CPY per rollback slot
(the slot order runs against the window order, so no single view covers
them) and then SSM_CONV(+SILU). For a single sequence and up to 16 tokens a
fused SSM_CONV now reads both CONCAT sources directly (the conv state
through the s_copy index from the cache), writes the snapshot windows into
the cache and convolves, so the CONCAT, the CPYs and the gather are elided:
qwen35 verify batches lose 7 launches per GDN layer.
The plan checks that every CONCAT reader is accounted for, that nothing
between the CONCAT and the SSM_CONV writes its sources or reads the cache
rows, and that the output does not alias the inputs. Each thread reads its
channel's inputs before writing a snapshot, so a slot row may be the source
row. The convolution arithmetic is unchanged (bitwise).
